translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.dot=. - Matches any character
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.dot.desc1=Matches any character
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.dot.desc2=The only exception is the newline character (\\n)
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.dot.desc3=Newlines are not used in chat so it doesn't matter

translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.word=\\w - Matches word
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.word.desc1=Matches all alphabets (Both capital and small), numbers and underscore
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.word.desc2=Minecraft usernames are based on words. They are perfect to detect player names

translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.digit=\\d - Digit
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.digit.desc1=Matches all numbers

translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.range=[a-g] - Match character in range
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.range.desc1=Matches any characters in this specific range
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.range.desc2=Example: [a-g]

translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.star=* - Matches 0 or more
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.star.desc1=Matches 0 or more of its character class
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.star.desc2=Example: N\\w*

translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.plus=+ - Matches 1 or more
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.plus.desc1=Matches 1 or more of a character/group
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.plus.desc2=Example: N\\w+

translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.optional=? - Optional
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.optional.desc1=Exactly as the name suggests
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.optional.desc2=Example: (VIP )?\\w+

translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.brace={2,} - Matches n or more
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.brace.desc1=Matches a group/character n times or more
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.brace.desc2=Add a number after the comma if you want it to match x to y times
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.brace.desc3=Or omit the comma if you want it to match exactly n times
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.brace.desc4=Example: Level \\d{1,3}

translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.either=| - Either
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.either.desc1=Must match either of them, but not both.
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.either.desc2=Example: (Dead)|(Alive) (\\w+)

translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.group=() - Group
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.group.desc1=Think of groups as parentheses like in mathematics
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.group.desc2=They also have a second function. Capture groups.
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.group.desc3=By specifying the group number below, the mod can know which group
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.group.desc4= contains the player's username

translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.escape=\\\\ - Escape character
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.escape.desc1=If you need to capture special characters mentioned in this list,
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.escape.desc2= you will need to add an extra backslash to escape them.
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.escape.correct=Correct:
translationmod.regex_gui.cheatsheet.escape.wrong=Wrong:

